From: Hadron BSP <support@connecttech.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: tegra: xusb-tegra186: do not reset VBUS/ID override to floating

NVIDIA's UTMI enable path resets the USB2_VBUS_ID VBUS/ID override to
floating, clobbering the override programmed from the USB role switch on
the Hadron OTG port. Drop that reset so the host-mode VBUS/ID override set
elsewhere sticks (Tegra234/Orin uses this driver).

Upstreamed from CTI L4T 36.4.4-V005 kernel source (in-tree delta).
--- a/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra186.c	2025-07-01 13:48:42.000000000 +0300
+++ b/drivers/phy/tegra/xusb-tegra186.c	2025-12-23 21:22:11.000000000 +0200
@@ -980,13 +980,6 @@
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
 
-	/* reset VBUS&ID OVERRIDE */
-	reg = padctl_readl(padctl, USB2_VBUS_ID);
-	reg &= ~VBUS_OVERRIDE;
-	reg &= ~ID_OVERRIDE(~0);
-	reg |= ID_OVERRIDE_FLOATING;
-	padctl_writel(padctl, reg, USB2_VBUS_ID);
-
 	if (port->supply && port->mode == USB_DR_MODE_HOST) {
 		err = regulator_enable(port->supply);
 		if (err) {
